<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28501" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlissa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλισσα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A nymph who is said to have invented the art of
				keeping bees</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 2,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Daughter of the Cretan king Melissus, who, together
				with her sister Amalthea, fed Jupiter with goats' milk</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 22, 19</span></i> sq</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>